CORE gcc-only
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ typeof subscript: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ typeof array type-id: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
GCC's typeof extension: `__typeof__(a[0])' names the type of the expression
a[0], but the parser reads it as the type-id "array of 0 a" and the front
end reported "found no match for symbol 'a'" (bin53).  As for sizeof
([dcl.ambig.res]/2), a name that does not denote a type makes the operand
the expression a[0]; `__typeof__(T[2])' with T a type stays a type-id.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
